<section id="Sx2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Detailed MAVEN-FACT Analysis</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data extraction.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">train</span> split of <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MAVEN-FACT</span> v1.0
(73,939 event–mentions drawn from 2 913 news
articles).<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            Available at
<a href="https://github.com/THU-KEG/MAVEN-FACT" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/THU-KEG/MAVEN-FACT</a>.</span></span></span>
Each mention carries a FactBank-style factuality code
(<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CT++</span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CT+</span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CT-</span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CT--</span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PS <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PR <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CF <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math></span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">U</span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NA</span>, …).
We retain only <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">certain</span> judgments:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{certain-true}=\{\text{CT++},\text{CT+}\},\qquad\text{certain-false}=\{\text{CT- -},\text{CT-}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>certain-true</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>CT++</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>CT+</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>certain-false</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>CT- -</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>CT-</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{certain-true}=\{\text{CT++},\text{CT+}\},\qquad\text{certain-false}=\{\text{CT- -},\text{CT-}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">All other codes are discarded, leaving
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=71,274" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>71,274</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=71,274</annotation></semantics></math> labelled mentions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Grouping key.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Mentions are grouped by their originating article
ID (<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">doc_id</span>), giving
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=2,913" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2,913</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=2,913</annotation></semantics></math> documents with at least two certain mentions
(<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>).
Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{ij}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{ij}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> indicate whether mention <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> in document <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>
is <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">certain-false</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Statistics reported in the main text.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corpus certain-false rate.</span> 
<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\tfrac{1}{N}\sum_{i,j}Z_{ij}=0.0209" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0209</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\tfrac{1}{N}\sum_{i,j}Z_{ij}=0.0209</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pairwise certain-false probability.</span> 
<math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr(Z_{j}=Z_{k}=1\mid\text{same doc})=\frac{\sum_{i}\binom{f_{i}}{2}}{\sum_{i}\binom{n_{i}}{2}}=0.00090," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mtext>same doc</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00090</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr(Z_{j}=Z_{k}=1\mid\text{same doc})=\frac{\sum_{i}\binom{f_{i}}{2}}{\sum_{i}\binom{n_{i}}{2}}=0.00090,</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}=\sum_{j}Z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}=\sum_{j}Z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Independence baseline.</span> 
<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{2}=0.00044" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.00044</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{2}=0.00044</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clustering ratio.</span> 
<math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\operatorname{Var}_{\text{obs}}(\hat{p}_{i})}{\operatorname{Var}_{\text{binom}}}=\frac{\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i}(\hat{p}_{i}-p)^{2}}{\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i}p(1-p)/n_{i}}=1.23\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mtext>obs</mtext></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mtext>binom</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>1.23</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\operatorname{Var}_{\text{obs}}(\hat{p}_{i})}{\operatorname{Var}_{\text{binom}}}=\frac{\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i}(\hat{p}_{i}-p)^{2}}{\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i}p(1-p)/n_{i}}=1.23\,,</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{i}=f_{i}/n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{i}=f_{i}/n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> test.</span> 
The <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times M</annotation></semantics></math> contingency table of
<math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f_{i},\,n_{i}-f_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f_{i},\,n_{i}-f_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> yields
<math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}=4\,174" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4 174</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}=4\,174</annotation></semantics></math>
(<math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\approx 9{\times}10^{-49}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>49</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\approx 9{\times}10^{-49}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These figures show that <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">certain-false</em> events, though rare
(<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.1\%</annotation></semantics></math>), occur about twice as often as chance would predict when two
events come from the same article, and the distribution of false rates
across articles is 23 % more heterogeneous than a binomial model would
permit—confirming the co-occurrence signal predicted by TCH.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The MAVEN-ED dataset is released with CC BY-SA 4.0 license. The MAVEN-ARG and MAVEN-ERE are published with GPLv3 license.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Entropy incentive</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider sequences <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y,x^{\prime},y^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y,x^{\prime},y^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> with subjects <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,x^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,x^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and attributes <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y,y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y,y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathcal{S}\to\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathcal{S}\to\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be the ground-truth attribute map.
A latent bit <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\!\sim\!\mathrm{Bernoulli}(\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\!\sim\!\mathrm{Bernoulli}(\rho)</annotation></semantics></math> governs whether attributes are truthful (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T{=}1</annotation></semantics></math>) or random (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T{=}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T{=}0</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T=1:\;y=g(x),\;y^{\prime}=g(x^{\prime})\quad\text{(deterministic)};\qquad T=0:\;y,y^{\prime}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathrm{Unif}(\mathcal{A})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>(deterministic)</mtext><mo rspace="2.167em">;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mover><mo>∼</mo><mtext>i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mi>Unif</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1:\;y=g(x),\;y^{\prime}=g(x^{\prime})\quad\text{(deterministic)};\qquad T=0:\;y,y^{\prime}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathrm{Unif}(\mathcal{A}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We study the optimal next-token loss for predicting <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> given the prefix <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y,x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y,x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> under two cases:
(i) the model <em id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">does not access</em> <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>; (ii) the model <em id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">does</em> access <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (and can memorize <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">A. Predictive distribution of <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> without access to <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the law of total probability over <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and the generator above,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\!\big(y^{\prime}=g(x^{\prime})\,\big|\,x,y,x^{\prime}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\!\big(y^{\prime}=g(x^{\prime})\,\big|\,x,y,x^{\prime}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Pr(T{=}1\,|\,x,y,x^{\prime})\cdot 1\;+\;\Pr(T{=}0\,|\,x,y,x^{\prime})\cdot\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Pr(T{=}1\,|\,x,y,x^{\prime})\cdot 1\;+\;\Pr(T{=}0\,|\,x,y,x^{\prime})\cdot\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When we say the model is “ignorant of <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>,” we mean it does not exploit any posterior signal about <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> from the prefix; thus we use the prior
<math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(T{=}1\,|\,x,y,x^{\prime})=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(T{=}1\,|\,x,y,x^{\prime})=\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(T{=}0\,|\,x,y,x^{\prime})=1-\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(T{=}0\,|\,x,y,x^{\prime})=1-\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\big(y^{\prime}=g(x^{\prime})\,\big|\,x,y,x^{\prime}\big)=\rho+\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\big(y^{\prime}=g(x^{\prime})\,\big|\,x,y,x^{\prime}\big)=\rho+\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For any <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">specific wrong</em> <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\!\in\!\mathcal{A}\setminus\{g(x^{\prime})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\!\in\!\mathcal{A}\setminus\{g(x^{\prime})\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\big(y^{\prime}=a\,\big|\,x,y,x^{\prime}\big)=\rho\cdot 0+(1-\rho)\cdot\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}=\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\big(y^{\prime}=a\,\big|\,x,y,x^{\prime}\big)=\rho\cdot 0+(1-\rho)\cdot\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}=\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">B. Optimal per-token cross-entropy without <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:=\rho+\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:=\rho+\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta:=\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta:=\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The optimal model (that does not access <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>) matches the true conditional in (<a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ A. Predictive distribution of 𝑦^′ without access to 𝑇 ‣ Appendix B Entropy incentive ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>)–(<a href="#A2.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ A. Predictive distribution of 𝑦^′ without access to 𝑇 ‣ Appendix B Entropy incentive ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), so its per-token cross-entropy equals the entropy of that distribution:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\neg T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\neg T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H\!\Big(\alpha,\underbrace{\beta,\ldots,\beta}_{|\mathcal{A}|-1\text{ times}}\Big)=-\alpha\log\alpha-(|\mathcal{A}|-1)\,\beta\log\beta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> times</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H\!\Big(\alpha,\underbrace{\beta,\ldots,\beta}_{|\mathcal{A}|-1\text{ times}}\Big)=-\alpha\log\alpha-(|\mathcal{A}|-1)\,\beta\log\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">C. Optimal per-token cross-entropy with access to <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If the model <em id="A2.SS0.SSSx3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">does</em> access <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> (and has memorized <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1:\ \text{loss }0\quad\text{(since }y^{\prime}=g(x^{\prime})\text{ deterministically)};\qquad T=0:\ \text{loss }\log|\mathcal{A}|\quad\text{(uniform on }\mathcal{A}\text{)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mtext>loss </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>(since </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> deterministically)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">;</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>loss </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>(uniform on </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1:\ \text{loss }0\quad\text{(since }y^{\prime}=g(x^{\prime})\text{ deterministically)};\qquad T=0:\ \text{loss }\log|\mathcal{A}|\quad\text{(uniform on }\mathcal{A}\text{)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Averaging over <math id="A2.SS0.SSSx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{T}=(1-\rho)\,\log|\mathcal{A}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{T}=(1-\rho)\,\log|\mathcal{A}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">D. The gap and its limit as <math id="A2.SSx1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{A}|\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{A}|\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A2.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Subtracting (<a href="#A2.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ C. Optimal per-token cross-entropy with access to 𝑇 ‣ Appendix B Entropy incentive ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) from (<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ B. Optimal per-token cross-entropy without 𝑇 ‣ Appendix B Entropy incentive ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathcal{L}_{\neg T}-\mathcal{L}_{T}=-\alpha\log\alpha-(|\mathcal{A}|-1)\beta\log\beta\;-\;(1-\rho)\log|\mathcal{A}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathcal{L}_{\neg T}-\mathcal{L}_{T}=-\alpha\log\alpha-(|\mathcal{A}|-1)\beta\log\beta\;-\;(1-\rho)\log|\mathcal{A}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A2.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-(|\mathcal{A}|-1)\beta\log\beta=-(1-\rho)\Big(1-\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\Big)\log(1-\rho)+(1-\rho)\Big(1-\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\Big)\log|\mathcal{A}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(|\mathcal{A}|-1)\beta\log\beta=-(1-\rho)\Big(1-\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\Big)\log(1-\rho)+(1-\rho)\Big(1-\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\Big)\log|\mathcal{A}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SSx1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Plugging into (<a href="#A2.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ D. The gap and its limit as |𝒜|→∞ ‣ Appendix B Entropy incentive ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) and simplifying,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\alpha\log\alpha\;-\;(1-\rho)\Big(1-\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\Big)\log(1-\rho)\;-\;\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}\,\log|\mathcal{A}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\alpha\log\alpha\;-\;(1-\rho)\Big(1-\tfrac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\Big)\log(1-\rho)\;-\;\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}\,\log|\mathcal{A}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SSx1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\rho+\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}\to\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\rho+\frac{1-\rho}{|\mathcal{A}|}\to\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and the last term is <math id="A2.SSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\tfrac{\log|\mathcal{A}|}{|\mathcal{A}|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\tfrac{\log|\mathcal{A}|}{|\mathcal{A}|})</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the limit</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\xrightarrow[|\mathcal{A}|\to\infty]{}\;-\rho\log\rho-(1-\rho)\log(1-\rho)\;\equiv\;H_{2}(\rho)\quad\text{(up to the log base).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒜</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(up to the log base).</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\xrightarrow[|\mathcal{A}|\to\infty]{}\;-\rho\log\rho-(1-\rho)\log(1-\rho)\;\equiv\;H_{2}(\rho)\quad\text{(up to the log base).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experimental Setup</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span>. We experiment with an attention-only transformer with a single attention head with a post-attention LN:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X^{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=E+P\quad\;\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.56em;" width="1.56em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=E+P\quad\;\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{// }E,P\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times d}\text{ (token + positional embeddings)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>// </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> (token + positional embeddings)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{// }E,P\in\mathbb{R}^{V\times d}\text{ (token + positional embeddings)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X^{(i-1)}W_{Q}^{(i)},K^{(i)}=X^{(i-1)}W_{K}^{(i)},V^{(i)}=X^{(i-1)}W_{V}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X^{(i-1)}W_{Q}^{(i)},K^{(i)}=X^{(i-1)}W_{K}^{(i)},V^{(i)}=X^{(i-1)}W_{V}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{softmax}\!\bigl(\tfrac{Q^{(i)}{K^{(i)}}^{\!\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\bigr)V^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.720em;" width="3.720em"><mi>softmax</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>K</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{softmax}\!\bigl(\tfrac{Q^{(i)}{K^{(i)}}^{\!\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\bigr)V^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{// attention mix }A^{(i)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>// attention mix </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{// attention mix }A^{(i)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{A}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{A}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=A^{(i)}W_{O}^{(i)},\quad W_{O}^{(i)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=A^{(i)}W_{O}^{(i)},\quad W_{O}^{(i)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.E23.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">// single-head attention output</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{N}\!\bigl(X^{(i-1)}+A^{(i)}\bigr),\qquad i=1,\dots,l\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>N</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{N}\!\bigl(X^{(i-1)}+A^{(i)}\bigr),\qquad i=1,\dots,l\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.E24.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">// residual + normalization</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=X^{(l)}W_{O}+b_{O},\quad W_{O}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times V},\;b_{O}\in\mathbb{R}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>O</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>V</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=X^{(l)}W_{O}+b_{O},\quad W_{O}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times V},\;b_{O}\in\mathbb{R}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{Y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{softmax}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{softmax}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experiments with one-hot models (<a href="#S4" title="4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)</span>. The theoretical analysis is driven by experiments on models equipped with frozen, one-hot embeddings and uniform attention, the latter obtained by setting the attention-key matrix <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to the zero matrix. Under these conditions the <em id="A3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">columns</em> of the attention value–output product <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="KV^{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KV^{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> map directly to individual vocabulary items, exposing a clear block structure in the matrix (<a href="#S4.F1" title="In Setup. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). As detailed in the main text, the vocabulary is organized so that indices 1–20 encode input subject embeddings, 21–40 input attribute embeddings, 41–44 positional embeddings, 45–64 output subject embeddings, and 65–84 output attribute embeddings.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Methodology: interpreting one-hot embeddings.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S4.F2" title="In Structure of the value matrix 𝑊. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> contrasts two sequences—a correct one (top row) and an incorrect one (bottom row)—by showing the final-layer activations before projecting to the logit space. The one-hot embeddings make the activation patterns in that layer interpretable. We display the activations for the raw representations (left), after layer normalization (middle), and after applying the unembedding matrix and the softmax transformation (right). Observe the differing <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>-axis scales: normalization substantially magnifies the component corresponding to the correct answer in the “true” sequence, while the effect is far less pronounced for the false sequence. The model that produced <a href="#S4.F1" title="In Setup. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> was trained with SGD, learning rate <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and batch size 16. The output matrix was fixed to identity, and only the value matrix was learned, from zero initialization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experiments with fully-trained models (<a href="#S5" title="5 Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)</span>: In <a href="#S5" title="5 Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we train all components, including the input embeddings and the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> attention matrix. The model is trained for 50,000 batches of size 128 and is optimized with the Adam optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma and Ba, 2015</a>]</cite> with a learning weight of 1e-4 and a weight decay of 1e-5. We do not include biases in the attention modules, and use RMSNorm as layer normalization. We run all experiments on 4 NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 GPUs. Training a single model lasts up to half an hour.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Experiments</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the main text we concentrated on a single-layer model (<math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1</annotation></semantics></math>) with a true-attribute probability of <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>. Here we extend the analysis to additional settings.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our primary focus was the linear separability at the second-subject token, <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the model predicts the second attribute. This is the only position where the truth signal is <em id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">behaviorally</em> relevant. Nevertheless, the theory also predicts a linear truth encoding at the first-attribute token <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, owing to the fixed attention pattern. When the attention <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="KV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KV</annotation></semantics></math> matrix is learned, however, this need not occur—the model can rely exclusively on the attention paid to <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and leave <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> uninformative. The same theory further implies that a linear truth direction should eventually emerge for any true-sentence rate <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, even though the gradient magnitude (and therefore the speed of emergence) does depend on <math id="A4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Varying the true sentence rate, <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> In <a href="#A4.F7.sf2" title="In Figure 7 ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7(b)</span></a> we vary <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> across five random seeds and measure linear separability at both token positions. As predicted, when the attention pattern is learned, separability is much stronger at the second subject than at the first attribute. The time to emergence grows as <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> increases, yet linear encoding still appears even at the extreme setting of <math id="A4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>. Developing a theory that precisely predicts this <math id="A4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent timing is left to future work.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="" id="A4.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_missing ltx_missing_image" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F7.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="" id="A4.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_missing ltx_missing_image" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F7.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A4.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Dependency of linear separability on <math id="A4.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F8.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.15804v1/auc_vs_n_d_tokeny.png" id="A4.F8.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/399;" width="476" height="399" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F8.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F8.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.15804v1/auc_vs_n_d_tokenx_prime.png" id="A4.F8.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/398;" width="476" height="398" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F8.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A4.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Dependency of linear separability on <math id="A4.F8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dependency on <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|</annotation></semantics></math></span>. In <a href="#A4.F8" title="In Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> we plot the linear separability at the final checkpoint, for different hidden sizes and number of facts to memorize (<math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed). With the exception of <math id="A4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}=32</annotation></semantics></math>, the separability persists over the second subject <math id="A4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for different combinations of these parameters.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15804v1/attn-3-layers.png" id="A4.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/159;" width="476" height="159" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A4.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">attention patterns of a 3-layer model.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F10.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.15804v1/First_layers3_p0.99.svg" id="A4.F10.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/298;" width="476" height="298"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F10.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F10.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.15804v1/Second_layers3_p0.99.svg" id="A4.F10.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/298;" width="476" height="298"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F10.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A4.F10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Linear separability across layers for a 3-layer model; linear separability on the <math id="A4.F10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> token is created after <em id="A4.F10.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">copying</em> the signal from the <math id="A4.F10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> token in the second layer.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Additional layers</span>. As we discuss in the main-text (<a href="#S5" title="5 Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), in a model with a single self-attention layer, it is the second attribute (<math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) token that attends to both <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. With more layers, there are additional strategies. For instance, <math id="A4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> may attend to both <math id="A4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and itself in the first layer, in the same way <math id="A4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> attends to both <math id="A4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> in the theoretical 1-layer model; then, in the next layer, <math id="A4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> attends to <math id="A4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, copies the signal and create a linear separation that persists the last layer. This is the mechanism that emerges in 4/5 random initializations of a 3-layer model, and is clearly manifested in the attention patterns (<a href="#A4.F9" title="In Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) and in the linear classification accuracy across layers (<a href="#A4.F10" title="In Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Bridging the gap between the fully-trainable model and the toy model.</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our theoretical analysis (<a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>) is motivated by the structured patterns that emerge in the attention kernel—the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OV</annotation></semantics></math> matrix—when it is visualized (<a href="#S4.F1" title="In Setup. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). To test whether a comparable mechanism appears when we employ dense embeddings and allow the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="KV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KV</annotation></semantics></math> matrices to train freely (thus removing the enforced uniform attention over <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y</annotation></semantics></math>), we train a model with a large hidden dimension but only a small set of facts to memorize (<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|=32</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}=512</annotation></semantics></math>). We freeze the randomly-initialized dense embeddings and train all other parameters. The limited number of subjects makes the memorization patterns easier to inspect, while the high dimensionality approximates the regime of mutually orthogonal embeddings required by the theory.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F11.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.15804v1/dot_product_kernel_frozen.png" id="A4.F11.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F11.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="A4.F11.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EVOE^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EVOE^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.F11.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> with frozen dense embeddings</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F11.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.15804v1/dot_product_kernel_unfrozen.png" id="A4.F11.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F11.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="A4.F11.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EVOE^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EVOE^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.F11.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> with trainable dense embeddings</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A4.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Visualization of the attention matrix with dense embeddings.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F12" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F12.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.15804v1/dot_product_kernel_frozen_firstk.png" id="A4.F12.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F12.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="A4.F12.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EVOE^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EVOE^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.F12.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> with frozen dense embeddings (sub-sampled and sorted)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F12.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.15804v1/dot_product_kernel_unfrozen_firstk.png" id="A4.F12.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F12.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="A4.F12.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EVOE^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EVOE^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.F12.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> with trainable dense embeddings (sub-sampled and sorted)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="A4.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Visualization of the attention matrix with dense embeddings.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because the model now uses dense embeddings—so individual coordinates no longer correspond directly to vocabulary items—we do not expect an obvious block structure in the raw <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OV</annotation></semantics></math> matrix. Instead, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dar et al. [2023]</a></cite>, we visualize <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EVOE^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EVOE^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> concatenates the input and output embedding matrices. This operation computes the pairwise similarities between embeddings as induced by the <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="VO" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">VO</annotation></semantics></math> transformation. Concretely, <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(EVOE^{\top})_{ij}=E_{i}^{\top}V,O,E_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(EVOE^{\top})_{ij}=E_{i}^{\top}V,O,E_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> measures how strongly the value vector elicited by symbol <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> aligns with the output direction that scores symbol <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, so every cell again describes a relation between concrete symbols, exactly what the raw <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OV</annotation></semantics></math> matrix showed when the embeddings were one-hot. The resulting heat-map (<a href="#A4.F11.sf1" title="In Figure 11 ‣ D.1 Bridging the gap between the fully-trainable model and the toy model. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11(a)</span></a>) exhibits a strikingly similar pattern to that observed with frozen one-hot embeddings and a fixed attention pattern, suggesting that the dense model converges to a similar underlying mechanism. In contrast, when we do train the embeddings, the pattern partially disappears, as parts of the memorization can occur in the embeddings themselves (<a href="#A4.F11.sf2" title="In Figure 11 ‣ D.1 Bridging the gap between the fully-trainable model and the toy model. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11(b)</span></a>). In general, there is much more variability between runs and hyperparameters when training the embeddings, where some hyperparameter choices do not show a pattern that is highly similar to the idealized one.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">With a full set of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|=d_{\text{model}}=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|=d_{\text{model}}=512</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, the global pattern is hard to spot at first glance.
If we instead sub-sample 28 <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, retain only their partners <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and then sort the rows/columns, the latent memorization re-emerges: the lower-left block collapses into a clear diagonal (the previously random pattern in the leftmost lower block in <a href="#A4.F11.sf1" title="In Figure 11 ‣ D.1 Bridging the gap between the fully-trainable model and the toy model. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11(a)</span></a> is transformed into a diagonal due to the sorting). This diagonal appears whether the embeddings are frozen or trainable (see <a href="#A4.F12.sf1" title="In Figure 12 ‣ D.1 Bridging the gap between the fully-trainable model and the toy model. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">figs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12(a)</span></a> and <a href="#A4.F12.sf2" title="Figure 12(b) ‣ Figure 12 ‣ D.1 Bridging the gap between the fully-trainable model and the toy model. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12(b)</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.15804v1/plots/learned_input_emb_small.jpg" id="A4.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:143/208;" width="143" height="208" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.15804v1/plots/ov_matrix_learned_onehot.png" id="A4.F13.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:238/198;" width="238" height="198" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F13.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="A4.F13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Visualization of learned embeddings and value matrix for a model as in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> with learned embeddings, initialized to one-hot.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">One possible circuit with learned embeddings.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now present one possible circuit that we found when initializing with the one-hot embeddings, in a simplified architecture with uniform attention as in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. We still denote <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{x},e_{y},u_{x},u_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{x},e_{y},u_{x},u_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> the one-hot embeddings as in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, which only refer to the initialization in this setting with learned embeddings.
After training, we may visualize the learned embeddings and interpret them as linear combinations of the initial one-hot embeddings, as shown in Figure <a href="#A4.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ D.1 Bridging the gap between the fully-trainable model and the toy model. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.
Denoting <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{e}_{x},\tilde{e}_{y},\tilde{u}_{x},\tilde{u}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{e}_{x},\tilde{e}_{y},\tilde{u}_{x},\tilde{u}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> the embeddings after training, the circuit we found looks as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{e}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{e}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e_{x}-e_{g(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e_{x}-e_{g(x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{e}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{e}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e_{y}-e_{g^{-1}(y)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e_{y}-e_{g^{-1}(y)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{u}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{u}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x}u_{x}-\sum_{y}u_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x}u_{x}-\sum_{y}u_{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{u}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{u}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{y}+e_{g^{-1}(y)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{y}+e_{g^{-1}(y)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x}(u_{g(x)}-e_{x})e_{x}^{\top}-\sum_{y}(e_{y}+u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x}(u_{g(x)}-e_{x})e_{x}^{\top}-\sum_{y}(e_{y}+u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The approximation <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{e}_{x}=e_{x}-e_{g(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{e}_{x}=e_{x}-e_{g(x)}</annotation></semantics></math>, for instance, follows from the two large positive and negative spikes in the left part of <a href="#A4.F13" title="In D.1 Bridging the gap between the fully-trainable model and the toy model. ‣ Appendix D Additional Experiments ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, for indices 1 and 25/36.
Similar to our analysis of Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we compute the quantity <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(\tilde{e}_{x}+\tilde{e}_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(\tilde{e}_{x}+\tilde{e}_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, which appears in the residual stream for both token <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and token <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W(\tilde{e}_{x}+\tilde{e}_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W(\tilde{e}_{x}+\tilde{e}_{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{g(x)}-e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+u_{g(x)}-e_{y}-u_{y}-u_{y}+e_{g^{-1}(y)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{g(x)}-e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+u_{g(x)}-e_{y}-u_{y}-u_{y}+e_{g^{-1}(y)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We observe that this vanishes when <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=g(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, suggesting that a similar mechanism as in the fixed embeddings case studied in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is at play, where layer-norm can lead to sharper predictions for true sequences, as well as provide a truth direction.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Theoretical analysis</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section contains theoretical analysis and proofs for the results in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Training dynamics</h3>

<figure id="A5.F14" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15804v1/ov_matrix_nopos.png" id="A5.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:238/195;" width="238" height="195" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F14.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 14</span>: </span><span id="A5.F14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Structure of the value matrix <math id="A5.F14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> when training without positional embeddings.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F15" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15804v1/W_euclidean.png" id="A5.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:238/238;" width="238" height="238" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F15.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 15</span>: </span><span id="A5.F15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Structure of the value matrix <math id="A5.F15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> when training with euclidean normalization.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now provide some theoretical insights on the training dynamics in the simple one-layer model of Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
We further simplify the model here by removing positional embeddings. Figure <a href="#A5.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ E.1 Training dynamics ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> shows that the model still learns the relevant blocks even without positional embeddings, though some of the uniform distributions on unembeddings are now absorbed in other blocks.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The lemma below highlights the structure of the gradient for a softmax classification model consisting of a linear model followed by a layer-norm operation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the model <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{W}(x)=U\cdot\mathsf{N}(a_{x}+Wb_{x})\in\mathbb{R}^{2N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{W}(x)=U\cdot\mathsf{N}(a_{x}+Wb_{x})\in\mathbb{R}^{2N}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{N}(v)=v/\|v\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{N}(v)=v/\|v\|</annotation></semantics></math>, and the following cross-entropy population loss on some distribution over <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(W)=\mathbb{E}_{x,y}[-\log\mathcal{S}(F_{W}(x))_{y}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(W)=\mathbb{E}_{x,y}[-\log\mathcal{S}(F_{W}(x))_{y}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is the label and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> the softmax operation.
The gradient with respect to <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is then given by:</span></p>
<table id="A5.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla L(W)=\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,y}\left[\frac{\mathcal{S}(U\cdot\mathsf{N}(v_{x}))_{k}-\mathbf{1}\{y=k\}}{\|v_{x}\|}\mathsf{P}_{(v_{x}/\|v_{x}\|)}u_{k}b_{x}^{\top}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝖭</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla L(W)=\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,y}\left[\frac{\mathcal{S}(U\cdot\mathsf{N}(v_{x}))_{k}-\mathbf{1}\{y=k\}}{\|v_{x}\|}\mathsf{P}_{(v_{x}/\|v_{x}\|)}u_{k}b_{x}^{\top}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{x}=a_{x}+Wb_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{x}=a_{x}+Wb_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and where <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{P}_{\theta}=I-\theta\theta^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖯</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{P}_{\theta}=I-\theta\theta^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection onto the tangent space at <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{S}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let us decompose the population loss as</p>
<table id="A5.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(W)=L_{1}(W)+L_{2}(W)+L_{3}(W)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(W)=L_{1}(W)+L_{2}(W)+L_{3}(W),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}(W)</annotation></semantics></math> is the next-token prediction loss for predicting <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{1:t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1:t}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{1:4}=(x,y,x^{\prime},y^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1:4}=(x,y,x^{\prime},y^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We show the following result.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the following algorithm, with step-size <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=N/\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=N/\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, and initialization <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Set </span><math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{1}=W_{0}-\eta\nabla L_{1}(W_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}=W_{0}-\eta\nabla L_{1}(W_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Set </span><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{2}=W_{1}-\eta\nabla L_{1}(W_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}=W_{1}-\eta\nabla L_{1}(W_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Set </span><math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{3}=W_{2}-\eta\nabla L_{3}(W_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{3}=W_{2}-\eta\nabla L_{3}(W_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{3}=\sum_{x=1}^{N}\left(\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}-\alpha_{1}e_{x}\right)e_{x}^{\top}+\sum_{y}(\alpha_{2}e_{g^{-1}(y)}-\beta_{2}u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(1/N)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{3}=\sum_{x=1}^{N}\left(\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}-\alpha_{1}e_{x}\right)e_{x}^{\top}+\sum_{y}(\alpha_{2}e_{g^{-1}(y)}-\beta_{2}u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(1/N),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1},\alpha_{2},\beta_{1},\beta_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1},\alpha_{2},\beta_{1},\beta_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> can be found in the proof, and <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> is a matrix where all entries are <math id="Thmtheorem3a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comment: Euclidean norm vs. RMS Norm.</span> The updates in this section are derived under Euclidean layer-norm <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(v)=v/\|v\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(v)=v/\|v\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the normalized scores entering the softmax are attenuated (compared to our experiments which use inverse temperature <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\sqrt{d}=\Theta(\sqrt{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\sqrt{d}=\Theta(\sqrt{N})</annotation></semantics></math>) by a factor of order <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\sqrt{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\sqrt{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, in the early regime with a fixed unembedding <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(N)</annotation></semantics></math> competing classes, the correct-token probability <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x,g(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x,g(x)}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>. In our implementation we use RMSNorm, <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{RMS}}(v)=\sqrt{d}\,\frac{v}{\|v\|_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>RMS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{RMS}}(v)=\sqrt{d}\,\frac{v}{\|v\|_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is equivalent to keeping Euclidean LN but applying a softmax with inverse temperature <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=\Theta(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=\Theta(N)</annotation></semantics></math> (here <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=4N+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=4N+3</annotation></semantics></math>), this multiplies every Euclidean score difference by <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{d}=\Theta(\sqrt{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{d}=\Theta(\sqrt{N})</annotation></semantics></math>, so relative advantages that were <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\sqrt{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\sqrt{N})</annotation></semantics></math> become <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, in the same early regime the correct-token probability becomes <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Empirically, we see similar structures emerge in the matrix during early training when using the euclidean norm instead of the RMS norm (<a href="#A5.F15" title="In E.1 Training dynamics ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us decompose each loss into contributions from true and false sequences, which follows from the fact that the data distribution is a mixture of the two:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}(W)=\rho L_{i}^{T}(W)+(1-\rho)L_{i}^{F}(W)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>F</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}(W)=\rho L_{i}^{T}(W)+(1-\rho)L_{i}^{F}(W).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the first step, we take a gradient step only on the loss <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for the prediction of the second token <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> at the first token <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, starting from initialization <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that this model takes the form <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)=U\cdot\mathsf{N}(e_{x}+We_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)=U\cdot\mathsf{N}(e_{x}+We_{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, so that in the notation of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ E.1 Training dynamics ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> we have <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{x}=b_{x}=v_{x}=e_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{x}=b_{x}=v_{x}=e_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{v_{x}/\|v_{x}\|}u_{k}=u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{v_{x}/\|v_{x}\|}u_{k}=u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that since the logits are all zero, we have <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(0)_{k}=\frac{1}{2N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(0)_{k}=\frac{1}{2N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with the gradient on true sequences. Multiplying <a href="#A5.E28" title="In Lemma 1. ‣ E.1 Training dynamics ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> by <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and setting <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=g(x)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{T}(W_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{T}(W_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\mathbb{E}_{x}[u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}]-\eta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathcal{S}(0)_{k}u_{k}\mathbb{E}_{x}[e_{x}^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\mathbb{E}_{x}[u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}]-\eta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathcal{S}(0)_{k}u_{k}\mathbb{E}_{x}[e_{x}^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}-\frac{\eta}{2N^{2}}\sum_{z=1}^{2N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{z}e_{x}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}-\frac{\eta}{2N^{2}}\sum_{z=1}^{2N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{z}e_{x}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">On false sequences, we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{F}(W_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>F</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{F}(W_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x}[\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathcal{S}(0)_{k}u_{k}e_{x}^{\top}]+\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,y}[u_{y}e_{x}^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x}[\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathcal{S}(0)_{k}u_{k}e_{x}^{\top}]+\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,y}[u_{y}e_{x}^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N^{2}}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}u_{y}e_{x}^{\top}-\frac{\eta}{2N^{2}}\sum_{z=1}^{2N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{z}e_{x}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N^{2}}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}u_{y}e_{x}^{\top}-\frac{\eta}{2N^{2}}\sum_{z=1}^{2N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{z}e_{x}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">using the fact that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> are independent.
With <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=N/\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=N/\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{1}=W_{0}-\eta\nabla L_{1}(W_{0})=\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(1/N)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}=W_{0}-\eta\nabla L_{1}(W_{0})=\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(1/N).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The second step is taken at <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=W_{1}=\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}+R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=W_{1}=\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}+R</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|R\|_{\infty}=O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|R\|_{\infty}=O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we have <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{x}=e_{x}+W_{1}e_{x}=e_{x}+u_{g(x)}+\varepsilon_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{x}=e_{x}+W_{1}e_{x}=e_{x}+u_{g(x)}+\varepsilon_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{\infty}=O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{\infty}=O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is one-hot, which implies <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}=O(1/\sqrt{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}=O(1/\sqrt{N})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also denote <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x,k}:=\mathcal{S}(U\cdot\mathsf{N}(v_{x}))_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x,k}:=\mathcal{S}(U\cdot\mathsf{N}(v_{x}))_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x,k}=O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x,k}=O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(u_{k}^{\top}\mathsf{N}(v_{x}))=\Theta(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(u_{k}^{\top}\mathsf{N}(v_{x}))=\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. On true sequences, we have:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{T}(W_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{T}(W_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\frac{1}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}}\left(I-\frac{v_{x}v_{x}^{\top}}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}^{2}}\right)u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}-\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\frac{\sigma_{x,k}}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}}\left(I-\frac{v_{x}v_{x}^{\top}}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}^{2}}\right)u_{k}e_{x}^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\frac{1}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}}\left(I-\frac{v_{x}v_{x}^{\top}}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}^{2}}\right)u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}-\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\frac{\sigma_{x,k}}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}}\left(I-\frac{v_{x}v_{x}^{\top}}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}^{2}}\right)u_{k}e_{x}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Note that we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|v_{x}\|=\sqrt{2+(e_{x}+u_{g(x)})^{\top}\varepsilon_{x}+\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}^{2}}=\sqrt{2+O(1/N)}=\sqrt{2}+O(1/N)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|v_{x}\|=\sqrt{2+(e_{x}+u_{g(x)})^{\top}\varepsilon_{x}+\|\varepsilon_{x}\|_{2}^{2}}=\sqrt{2+O(1/N)}=\sqrt{2}+O(1/N).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">by Taylor expansion. Then,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{x,k}:=\frac{1}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}}\left(I-\frac{v_{x}v_{x}^{\top}}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}^{2}}\right)u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{x,k}:=\frac{1}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}}\left(I-\frac{v_{x}v_{x}^{\top}}{\|v_{x}\|_{2}^{2}}\right)u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}+O(\frac{1}{N})}u_{k}+\frac{\delta_{k,g(x)}+O(\frac{1}{N})}{2\sqrt{2}+O(\frac{1}{N})}v_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}+O(\frac{1}{N})}u_{k}+\frac{\delta_{k,g(x)}+O(\frac{1}{N})}{2\sqrt{2}+O(\frac{1}{N})}v_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}u_{k}+\frac{\delta_{k,g(x)}}{2}(e_{x}+u_{g(x)})+O_{\infty}(1/N)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}u_{k}+\frac{\delta_{k,g(x)}}{2}(e_{x}+u_{g(x)})+O_{\infty}(1/N),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta_{k,g(x)}=\mathbf{1}\{k=g(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k,g(x)}=\mathbf{1}\{k=g(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Kronecker delta.
Plugging back into the gradient above, we obtain</p>
<table id="A5.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{T}(W_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{T}(W_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N\sqrt{2}}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\left(u_{g(x)}-\frac{1}{2}(e_{x}+u_{g(x)})+O_{\infty}\left(\frac{1}{N}\right)\right)e_{x}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N\sqrt{2}}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\left(u_{g(x)}-\frac{1}{2}(e_{x}+u_{g(x)})+O_{\infty}\left(\frac{1}{N}\right)\right)e_{x}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\frac{\eta}{N\sqrt{2}}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\sigma_{x,k}v_{x,k}e_{x}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\frac{\eta}{N\sqrt{2}}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\sigma_{x,k}v_{x,k}e_{x}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{2\sqrt{2}N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}(u_{g(x)}-e_{x})e_{x}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{2\sqrt{2}N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}(u_{g(x)}-e_{x})e_{x}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which follows by noticing that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\sigma_{x,k}v_{x,k}=O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\sigma_{x,k}v_{x,k}=O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For false sequences, we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{F}(W_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>F</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{1}^{F}(W_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,y}[v_{x,y}e_{x}^{\top}]-\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\sigma_{x,k}v_{x,k}e_{x}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,y}[v_{x,y}e_{x}^{\top}]-\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\sigma_{x,k}v_{x,k}e_{x}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N^{2}}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}v_{x,y}e_{x}^{\top}-\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\sigma_{x,k}v_{x,k}e_{x}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\eta}{N^{2}}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}v_{x,y}e_{x}^{\top}-\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\sigma_{x,k}v_{x,k}e_{x}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">This again follows by noticing that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}v_{x,y}=O_{\infty}(1/N)\quad\text{and}\quad\sum_{k=1}^{2N}v_{x,k}=O_{\infty}(1/N)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}v_{x,y}=O_{\infty}(1/N)\quad\text{and}\quad\sum_{k=1}^{2N}v_{x,k}=O_{\infty}(1/N).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=N/\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=N/\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, this yields</p>
<table id="A5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{2}=W_{1}-\eta\nabla L_{1}(W_{1})=\sum_{t=1}^{N}\left(\alpha u_{g(t)}-e_{t}\right)e_{t}^{\top}+O(1/N)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}=W_{1}-\eta\nabla L_{1}(W_{1})=\sum_{t=1}^{N}\left(\alpha u_{g(t)}-e_{t}\right)e_{t}^{\top}+O(1/N),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1+\frac{1}{2\sqrt{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1+\frac{1}{2\sqrt{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The third step takes one gradient step on the loss <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> at the third token, i.e., predicting <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y,x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y,x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The model now takes the form <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x,y,x^{\prime})=U\cdot\mathsf{N}(e_{x^{\prime}}+\frac{1}{3}W(e_{x}+e_{y}+e_{x^{\prime}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x,y,x^{\prime})=U\cdot\mathsf{N}(e_{x^{\prime}}+\frac{1}{3}W(e_{x}+e_{y}+e_{x^{\prime}}))</annotation></semantics></math>, with a uniform attention on the first three tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We get the gradient of the loss on <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A5.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Lemma 1. ‣ E.1 Training dynamics ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), giving<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              We use the fact <math id="footnote5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}e_{t}=\alpha u_{g(t)}-e_{t}+O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}e_{t}=\alpha u_{g(t)}-e_{t}+O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="footnote5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</span></span></span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e_{x^{\prime}}+\frac{1}{3}W_{2}(e_{x}+e_{y}+e_{x^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e_{x^{\prime}}+\frac{1}{3}W_{2}(e_{x}+e_{y}+e_{x^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2}{3}e_{x^{\prime}}-\frac{1}{3}e_{x}+\frac{\alpha}{3}u_{g(x)}+\frac{\alpha}{3}u_{g(x^{\prime})}+\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}=:v_{x,x^{\prime}}+\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2}{3}e_{x^{\prime}}-\frac{1}{3}e_{x}+\frac{\alpha}{3}u_{g(x)}+\frac{\alpha}{3}u_{g(x^{\prime})}+\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}=:v_{x,x^{\prime}}+\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|_{\infty}=O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|_{\infty}=O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>, since it is the sum of 3 columns of the <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> term in <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
As in the second step, we have <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|_{2}^{2}=O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|_{2}^{2}=O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}=O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}=O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that by Taylor expansion we have <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|=\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|+O(1/N)=\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{5+2\alpha^{2}}+O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|=\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|+O(1/N)=\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{5+2\alpha^{2}}+O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|=\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|+O(1/N)=\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{1+2\alpha^{2}}+O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|=\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|+O(1/N)=\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{1+2\alpha^{2}}+O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that we once again have <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{x,y,x^{\prime},k}:=\mathcal{S}(U\cdot\mathsf{N}(v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}))_{k}=O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{x,y,x^{\prime},k}:=\mathcal{S}(U\cdot\mathsf{N}(v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}))_{k}=O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> due to the normalization. On true sequences, we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{3}^{T}(W_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{3}^{T}(W_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\eta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}}{3\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\eta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}}{3\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Let us first show that the error terms <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> lead to negligible contributions to the gradient. Note that we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{x,y,x^{\prime},k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{x,y,x^{\prime},k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,y,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{3(\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|+O(\frac{1}{N}))}\left(I-\frac{(v_{x,x^{\prime}}+O_{\infty}(\frac{1}{N}))(v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\frac{1}{N}))}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}+O(\frac{1}{N})}\right)u_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{3(\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|+O(\frac{1}{N}))}\left(I-\frac{(v_{x,x^{\prime}}+O_{\infty}(\frac{1}{N}))(v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\frac{1}{N}))}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}+O(\frac{1}{N})}\right)u_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}+\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime},k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}+\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime},k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime},k}\|_{\infty}=O(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon_{x,y,x^{\prime},k}\|_{\infty}=O(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>, where we used <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{a+\epsilon}=\frac{1}{a}+O(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{a+\epsilon}=\frac{1}{a}+O(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u+\epsilon)(u^{T}+\epsilon)=uu^{T}+O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u+\epsilon)(u^{T}+\epsilon)=uu^{T}+O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then, taking expectations with respect to independent <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is easy to check that</p>
<table id="A5.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\varepsilon_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}]=O_{\infty}(1/N^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\varepsilon_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}]=O_{\infty}(1/N^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}\varepsilon_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}]=O_{\infty}(1/N^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}\varepsilon_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}]=O_{\infty}(1/N^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The gradient update can then be rewritten as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{3}^{T}(W_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta\nabla L_{3}^{T}(W_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\eta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\eta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">We now check that the second term is also of order <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, the projector matrix <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is sparse with rows of bounded <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> norm, and we have <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}u_{k}=O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}u_{k}=O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\frac{\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}=:\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}=O_{\infty}(1/N)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\frac{\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}=:\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}=O_{\infty}(1/N),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{2N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{2N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{\sigma_{x,g(x),x^{\prime},k}}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{k}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}e_{x}^{\top}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}e_{g(x)}^{\top}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}e_{x^{\prime}}^{\top}=O_{\infty}(1/N^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}e_{x}^{\top}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}e_{g(x)}^{\top}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}\zeta_{x,x^{\prime}}e_{x^{\prime}}^{\top}=O_{\infty}(1/N^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.5" class="ltx_p">For the first term (<a href="#A5.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Step 3. ‣ E.1 Training dynamics ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}\left(I-\frac{v_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}^{\top}}{\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{2}}\right)u_{g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{*}{=}\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}u_{g(x^{\prime})}e_{x^{\prime}}^{\top}\right]+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{\alpha(1+\delta_{g(x),g(x^{\prime})})}{9\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{3}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{*}{=}\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}u_{g(x^{\prime})}e_{x^{\prime}}^{\top}\right]+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\frac{\alpha(1+\delta_{g(x),g(x^{\prime})})}{9\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{3}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\eta\beta_{1}}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\eta\beta_{1}}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.6" class="ltx_p">with</p>
<table id="A5.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{1}=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,1}\|}]\quad\text{ and }\quad\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}=\frac{\alpha(1+\delta_{g(x),g(x^{\prime})})}{9\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{3}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{1}=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\frac{1}{3\|v_{x,1}\|}]\quad\text{ and }\quad\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}=\frac{\alpha(1+\delta_{g(x),g(x^{\prime})})}{9\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(*)</annotation></semantics></math> we used (i) that
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\tfrac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}u_{g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)})^{\top}]=O_{\infty}(1/N^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\tfrac{1}{3\|v_{x,x^{\prime}}\|}u_{g(x^{\prime})}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)})^{\top}]=O_{\infty}(1/N^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> thanks to the independence of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>; and (ii) the fact that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{g(x^{\prime})}^{T}v_{x,x^{\prime}}=\frac{\alpha}{3}(1+\delta_{g(x),g(x^{\prime})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{g(x^{\prime})}^{T}v_{x,x^{\prime}}=\frac{\alpha}{3}(1+\delta_{g(x),g(x^{\prime})})</annotation></semantics></math> by definition of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{x,x^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{x,x^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and thanks to orthogonality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\eta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}\left[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}(e_{x}+e_{g(x)}+e_{x^{\prime}})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x}[\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}|x](e_{x}+e_{g(x)})^{\top}]-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\mathbb{E}_{x}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}|x^{\prime}]e_{x^{\prime}}^{\top}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x}[\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}|x](e_{x}+e_{g(x)})^{\top}]-\eta\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\mathbb{E}_{x}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}|x^{\prime}]e_{x^{\prime}}^{\top}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{*}{=}\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}(e_{x}-\alpha u_{g(x)})(e_{x}+e_{g(x)})^{\top}-\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}(2e_{x}+\alpha u_{g(x)})e_{x}^{\top}+O(\eta/N^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{*}{=}\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}(e_{x}-\alpha u_{g(x)})(e_{x}+e_{g(x)})^{\top}-\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}(2e_{x}+\alpha u_{g(x)})e_{x}^{\top}+O(\eta/N^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{**}{=}-\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}e_{x}e_{x}^{\top}+\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}(e_{g^{-1}(y)}-\alpha u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∗</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{**}{=}-\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}e_{x}e_{x}^{\top}+\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}(e_{g^{-1}(y)}-\alpha u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">with</p>
<table id="A5.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{2}=\frac{1}{3}\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{1,x^{\prime}}]=\frac{1}{3}\mathbb{E}_{x}[\gamma_{x,1}]=\frac{1}{3N}\gamma_{1,1}+\frac{N-1}{3N}\gamma_{1,2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{2}=\frac{1}{3}\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{1,x^{\prime}}]=\frac{1}{3}\mathbb{E}_{x}[\gamma_{x,1}]=\frac{1}{3N}\gamma_{1,1}+\frac{N-1}{3N}\gamma_{1,2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(*)</annotation></semantics></math> we condition on <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and decompose <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{x,x^{\prime}}=A(x)+B(x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{x,x^{\prime}}=A(x)+B(x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>; then linearity gives <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}\mid x]=A(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}]+\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}B(x^{\prime})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}v_{x,x^{\prime}}\mid x]=A(x)\,\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}]+\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}B(x^{\prime})]</annotation></semantics></math>.
By permutation symmetry of labels, <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}]=\mathbb{E}_{z}[\gamma_{1,z}]=3\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\gamma_{x,x^{\prime}}]=\mathbb{E}_{z}[\gamma_{1,z}]=3\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> part averages over a uniformly random index and is <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{\infty}(1/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{\infty}(1/N)</annotation></semantics></math>; the same holds with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> swapped for the second bracket.
Substituting these two conditionals into the split expectation, replacing outer expectations by uniform sums, and renaming the dummy index yields the displayed <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(*)</annotation></semantics></math> line. In <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(**)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(**)</annotation></semantics></math> we perform change of variables <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=g(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have thus shown</p>
<table id="A5.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\eta\nabla L_{3}^{T}(W_{2})=\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}(\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}-\beta_{2}e_{x})e_{x}^{\top}+\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}(e_{g^{-1}(y)}-\alpha u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\eta\nabla L_{3}^{T}(W_{2})=\frac{\eta}{N}\sum_{x=1}^{N}(\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}-\beta_{2}e_{x})e_{x}^{\top}+\frac{\eta\beta_{2}}{N}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}(e_{g^{-1}(y)}-\alpha u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For false sequences, it can be checked that <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\eta\nabla L_{3}^{F}(W_{2})=O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>F</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\nabla L_{3}^{F}(W_{2})=O_{\infty}(\eta/N^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, taking step-size <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=N/\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=N/\rho</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A5.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{2}-\eta\nabla L_{3}(W_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{2}-\eta\nabla L_{3}(W_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\alpha+\beta_{1})\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}-(1+\beta_{2})\sum_{x=1}^{N}e_{x}e_{x}^{\top}+\beta_{2}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}(e_{g^{-1}}(y)-\alpha u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(1/N)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\alpha+\beta_{1})\sum_{x=1}^{N}u_{g(x)}e_{x}^{\top}-(1+\beta_{2})\sum_{x=1}^{N}e_{x}e_{x}^{\top}+\beta_{2}\sum_{y=N+1}^{2N}(e_{g^{-1}}(y)-\alpha u_{y})e_{y}^{\top}+O_{\infty}(1/N).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.1.1 </span>Learning (positional) attention.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now turn to learning the key–query matrix under positional attention, assuming that the value matrix has already been learned with the structure described above. Specifically, we show that the gradient of the key–query matrix on true sequences drives positional attention to focus on the <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> token, effectively causing the model to ignore the initial <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> pair. This observation may account for the absence of emergence at <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1</annotation></semantics></math>, although it does not explain why emergence still occurs when attention is trainable and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For this part, assume a simple architecture of the following form for the prediction of the fourth token logits given the first three tokens:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F_{W_{KQ}}(z_{1:3})=U\cdot\sum_{t=1}^{3}\frac{\exp(p_{t}^{\top}W_{KQ}p_{3})}{\sum_{t^{\prime}=1}^{3}\exp(p_{t^{\prime}}^{\top}W_{KQ}p_{3})}W_{V}e_{z_{t}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{W_{KQ}}(z_{1:3})=U\cdot\sum_{t=1}^{3}\frac{\exp(p_{t}^{\top}W_{KQ}p_{3})}{\sum_{t^{\prime}=1}^{3}\exp(p_{t^{\prime}}^{\top}W_{KQ}p_{3})}W_{V}e_{z_{t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{1:3}=(e_{x},e_{y},e_{x^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1:3}=(e_{x},e_{y},e_{x^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{1:3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1:3}</annotation></semantics></math> are the positional embeddings defined in (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Setup. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We assume <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed to the the structure in (<a href="#S4.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Structure of the value matrix 𝑊. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)-(<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Structure of the value matrix 𝑊. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=:\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}=:\beta</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity. We consider the following population loss for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{KQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{KQ}</annotation></semantics></math> on the last token for true sequences:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(W_{KQ})=\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\ell(g(x^{\prime}),F_{W_{KQ}}(x,g(x),x^{\prime}))]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(W_{KQ})=\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\ell(g(x^{\prime}),F_{W_{KQ}}(x,g(x),x^{\prime}))].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then, the negative gradient direction at <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{KQ}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{KQ}=0</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A5.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\nabla L(W_{KQ})=\frac{1}{3}\sum_{t=1}^{3}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))u_{k}^{\top}W_{V}e_{z_{t}}(p_{t}-\bar{p}_{1:3})p_{3}^{\top}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\nabla L(W_{KQ})=\frac{1}{3}\sum_{t=1}^{3}\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))u_{k}^{\top}W_{V}e_{z_{t}}(p_{t}-\bar{p}_{1:3})p_{3}^{\top}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where we denote <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{1:3}=(x,g(x),x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1:3}=(x,g(x),x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{p}_{1:3}=\frac{1}{3}(p_{1}+p_{2}+p_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}_{1:3}=\frac{1}{3}(p_{1}+p_{2}+p_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}</annotation></semantics></math> are probability predictions at <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{KQ}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{KQ}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which we assume satisfy the following, given the assumed structure on <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, for some small <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>:<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">6</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              This requires that we the early phase is run for long enough so that <math id="footnote6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough, say <math id="footnote6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log N)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime})=\begin{cases}(1-\epsilon)/2,&amp;\text{if }k\in\{g(x),g(x^{\prime})\}\text{ and }x\neq x^{\prime},\\
1-\epsilon,&amp;\text{if }k=g(x)\text{ and }x=x^{\prime},\\
O(1/N),&amp;\text{o/w}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>o/w</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime})=\begin{cases}(1-\epsilon)/2,&amp;\text{if }k\in\{g(x),g(x^{\prime})\}\text{ and }x\neq x^{\prime},\\
1-\epsilon,&amp;\text{if }k=g(x)\text{ and }x=x^{\prime},\\
O(1/N),&amp;\text{o/w}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let us now write the update in (<a href="#A5.E35" title="Equation 35 ‣ E.1.1 Learning (positional) attention. ‣ E.1 Training dynamics ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) as</p>
<table id="A5.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\nabla L(W_{KQ})=\frac{1}{3}\sum_{t=1}^{3}w_{t}(p_{t}-\bar{p}_{1:3})p_{3}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\nabla L(W_{KQ})=\frac{1}{3}\sum_{t=1}^{3}w_{t}(p_{t}-\bar{p}_{1:3})p_{3}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and study the values of the <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))u_{k}^{\top}W_{V}e_{x}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))u_{k}^{\top}W_{V}e_{x}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))\mathbf{1}\{g(x)=k\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))\mathbf{1}\{g(x)=k\}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\sum_{k=N+1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x}[\mathbf{1}\{g(x)=k\}]\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}]-\beta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\hat{p}(g(x)|x,x^{\prime})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\sum_{k=N+1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x}[\mathbf{1}\{g(x)=k\}]\mathbb{E}_{x^{\prime}}[\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}]-\beta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\hat{p}(g(x)|x,x^{\prime})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\beta}{N}-\frac{\beta}{N}(1-\epsilon)-\frac{\beta(N^{2}-N)}{N^{2}}\frac{1-\epsilon}{2}\leq-\beta\frac{1-\epsilon}{2}+O(\beta/N)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\beta}{N}-\frac{\beta}{N}(1-\epsilon)-\frac{\beta(N^{2}-N)}{N^{2}}\frac{1-\epsilon}{2}\leq-\beta\frac{1-\epsilon}{2}+O(\beta/N).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))u_{k}^{\top}W_{V}e_{g(x)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))u_{k}^{\top}W_{V}e_{g(x)}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\beta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))\mathbf{1}\{x=k\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>β</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\beta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))\mathbf{1}\{x=k\}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0+\beta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\hat{p}(x|x,x^{\prime})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0+\beta\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\hat{p}(x|x,x^{\prime})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O(\beta/N)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O(\beta/N).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=3</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex71.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))u_{k}^{\top}W_{V}e_{x^{\prime}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))u_{k}^{\top}W_{V}e_{x^{\prime}}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\sum_{k=1}^{2N}\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[(\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}-\hat{p}(k|x,x^{\prime}))\mathbf{1}\{g(x^{\prime})=k\}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta-\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\hat{p}(g(x^{\prime})|x,x^{\prime})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta-\mathbb{E}_{x,x^{\prime}}[\hat{p}(g(x^{\prime})|x,x^{\prime})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\beta-\beta\frac{1-\epsilon}{2}\geq\frac{\beta}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\beta-\beta\frac{1-\epsilon}{2}\geq\frac{\beta}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, when <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\gg\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≫</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\gg\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{3}-w_{1},w_{3}-w_{2}\geq\beta/2+O(\beta/N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{3}-w_{1},w_{3}-w_{2}\geq\beta/2+O(\beta/N)</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{KQ}^{1}=-\eta\nabla L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{KQ}^{1}=-\eta\nabla L</annotation></semantics></math>, the gap in attention logits between <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2</annotation></semantics></math> is of order <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\beta/6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\beta/6</annotation></semantics></math>, so that for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> large enough, the attention mostly focuses on the third token <math id="A5.SS1.SSS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Sharpening of 𝑦^′ predictions). ‣ Linear separation and sharpening mechanism. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose we are given <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y,x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y,x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, where we assume for simplicity that <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x^{\prime})\neq y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x^{\prime})\neq y</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{W}(z_{1:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{W}(z_{1:t})</annotation></semantics></math> the output of the model in (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Setup. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) before applying the LN and the unembedding layer. Then, we have that:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A5.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{W}(x,y,x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{W}(x,y,x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e_{x^{\prime}}+p_{3}+\frac{1}{3}\bar{\gamma}\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e_{x^{\prime}}+p_{3}+\frac{1}{3}\bar{\gamma}\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{3}\left(-\alpha_{1}e_{x}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}+\alpha_{2}e_{g^{-1}(y)}-\beta_{2}u_{y}-\alpha_{1}e_{x^{\prime}}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x^{\prime})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{3}\left(-\alpha_{1}e_{x}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}+\alpha_{2}e_{g^{-1}(y)}-\beta_{2}u_{y}-\alpha_{1}e_{x^{\prime}}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x^{\prime})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Denote by <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}:=2+\frac{\bar{\gamma}^{2}(2N-2)+2\alpha_{1}^{2}+\beta_{1}^{2}}{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}:=2+\frac{\bar{\gamma}^{2}(2N-2)+2\alpha_{1}^{2}+\beta_{1}^{2}}{9}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}:=2+\frac{\bar{\gamma}^{2}(2N-3)+2\alpha_{1}^{2}+\beta_{1}^{2}}{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}:=2+\frac{\bar{\gamma}^{2}(2N-3)+2\alpha_{1}^{2}+\beta_{1}^{2}}{9}</annotation></semantics></math> .
for a true sample where <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=g(x)</annotation></semantics></math> we have that:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert f_{W}(x,g(x),x^{\prime})\right\rVert^{2}=c+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}~." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert f_{W}(x,g(x),x^{\prime})\right\rVert^{2}=c+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, after applying the LN and unembedding layer we have that:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(F_{W}(x,g(x),x^{\prime}))_{g(x^{\prime})}=\frac{\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma}}{3\sqrt{c_{1}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(F_{W}(x,g(x),x^{\prime}))_{g(x^{\prime})}=\frac{\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma}}{3\sqrt{c_{1}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{y^{\prime}\neq g(x^{\prime})}(F_{W}(x,g(x),x^{\prime}))_{y^{\prime}}=\frac{\bar{\gamma}+\max(0,\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})}{3\sqrt{c_{1}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{y^{\prime}\neq g(x^{\prime})}(F_{W}(x,g(x),x^{\prime}))_{y^{\prime}}=\frac{\bar{\gamma}+\max(0,\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})}{3\sqrt{c_{1}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For a false sample where <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\neq g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\neq g(x)</annotation></semantics></math> we have that:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A5.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert f_{W}(x,g(x),x^{\prime})\right\rVert^{2}=c_{2}+2(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}~." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert f_{W}(x,g(x),x^{\prime})\right\rVert^{2}=c_{2}+2(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, after applying the LN and unembedding layer we have that:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(F_{W}(x,y,x^{\prime}))_{g(x^{\prime})}=\frac{\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma}}{3\sqrt{c_{2}+2(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(F_{W}(x,y,x^{\prime}))_{g(x^{\prime})}=\frac{\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma}}{3\sqrt{c_{2}+2(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{y^{\prime}\neq g(x^{\prime})}(F_{W}(x,y,x^{\prime}))_{y^{\prime}}=\frac{\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma}}{3\sqrt{c_{2}+2(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}}}~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{y^{\prime}\neq g(x^{\prime})}(F_{W}(x,y,x^{\prime}))_{y^{\prime}}=\frac{\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma}}{3\sqrt{c_{2}+2(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}}}~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Plugging in these terms finishes the proof.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Linear truth direction). ‣ Linear separation and sharpening mechanism. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<figure id="A5.F16" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15804v1/plots/2d_rmsnorm_side_by_side_biglegendxlabel.png" id="A5.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:357/184;" width="357" height="184" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F16.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 16</span>: </span><span id="A5.F16.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration for a LN-induced linear separability.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first describe the output of the model in (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Setup. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) before applying LN. Denote by <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{T},~v_{F}\in\mathbb{R}^{4N+3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{T},~v_{F}\in\mathbb{R}^{4N+3}</annotation></semantics></math> these outputs for true and false samples respectively. Recall that a true sample <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is when <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=g(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and false otherwise. Then, we have that:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{T}=e_{y}+p_{2}+\frac{1}{2}\left((\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})e_{x}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})u_{y}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})\cdot\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{T}=e_{y}+p_{2}+\frac{1}{2}\left((\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})e_{x}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})u_{y}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})\cdot\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{F}=e_{y}+p_{2}+\frac{1}{2}\left(-\alpha_{1}e_{x}+\alpha_{2}e_{g^{-1}(y)}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}-\beta_{2}u_{y}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})\cdot\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{F}=e_{y}+p_{2}+\frac{1}{2}\left(-\alpha_{1}e_{x}+\alpha_{2}e_{g^{-1}(y)}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}-\beta_{2}u_{y}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})\cdot\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">We will first show that without adding <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{N}</annotation></semantics></math> the samples above cannot be separated for general <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume otherwise, that there exists a linear separator <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=\begin{pmatrix}w_{1}\\
w_{2}\\
w_{3}\\
w_{4}\\
w_{5}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\begin{pmatrix}w_{1}\\
w_{2}\\
w_{3}\\
w_{4}\\
w_{5}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1},\dots,w_{4}\in\mathbb{R}^{N},w_{5}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1},\dots,w_{4}\in\mathbb{R}^{N},w_{5}\in\mathbb{R}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> and bias term <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle w,v_{T}\right\rangle-b\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle w,v_{T}\right\rangle-b\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle w,v_{F}\right\rangle-b&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle w,v_{F}\right\rangle-b&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for every true or false sample respectively. We slightly abuse notation and write <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle w_{1},e_{x}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle w_{1},e_{x}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\begin{pmatrix}w_{1}\\
0_{3N+3}\end{pmatrix},e_{x}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\begin{pmatrix}w_{1}\\
0_{3N+3}\end{pmatrix},e_{x}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, and similarly when multiplying <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:=\frac{1}{2}\left\langle(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})\cdot\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right),w_{3}+w_{4}\right\rangle+\left\langle w_{5},p_{2}\right\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:=\frac{1}{2}\left\langle(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})\cdot\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right),w_{3}+w_{4}\right\rangle+\left\langle w_{5},p_{2}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">the terms in the inner products that are independent of the sample. Then, using the linear separator on these four samples we have:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b\leq(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})\left\langle e_{x_{i}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{i}}w_{2}\right\rangle+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})\left\langle u_{y_{i}},w_{4}\right\rangle+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b\leq(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})\left\langle e_{x_{i}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{i}}w_{2}\right\rangle+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})\left\langle u_{y_{i}},w_{4}\right\rangle+c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b\leq(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})\left\langle e_{x_{j}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{j}}w_{2}\right\rangle+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})\left\langle u_{y_{j}},w_{4}\right\rangle+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b\leq(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})\left\langle e_{x_{j}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{j}}w_{2}\right\rangle+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})\left\langle u_{y_{j}},w_{4}\right\rangle+c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b\geq\alpha_{2}\left\langle e_{x_{i}},w_{1}\right\rangle-\alpha_{1}\left\langle e_{x_{j}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{i}},w_{2}\right\rangle+\beta_{1}\left\langle u_{y_{j}},w_{4}\right\rangle-\beta_{2}\left\langle u_{y_{i}},w_{4}\right\rangle+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b\geq\alpha_{2}\left\langle e_{x_{i}},w_{1}\right\rangle-\alpha_{1}\left\langle e_{x_{j}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{i}},w_{2}\right\rangle+\beta_{1}\left\langle u_{y_{j}},w_{4}\right\rangle-\beta_{2}\left\langle u_{y_{i}},w_{4}\right\rangle+c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b\geq\alpha_{2}\left\langle e_{x_{j}},w_{1}\right\rangle-\alpha_{1}\left\langle e_{x_{i}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{j}},w_{2}\right\rangle+\beta_{1}\left\langle u_{y_{i}},w_{4}\right\rangle-\beta_{2}\left\langle u_{y_{j}},w_{4}\right\rangle+c~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b\geq\alpha_{2}\left\langle e_{x_{j}},w_{1}\right\rangle-\alpha_{1}\left\langle e_{x_{i}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{j}},w_{2}\right\rangle+\beta_{1}\left\langle u_{y_{i}},w_{4}\right\rangle-\beta_{2}\left\langle u_{y_{j}},w_{4}\right\rangle+c~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Adding up (<a href="#A5.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ Proof. ‣ E.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ Proof. ‣ E.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) we have that:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2b-2c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2b-2c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})\left\langle e_{x_{j}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{j}}w_{2}\right\rangle+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})\left\langle u_{y_{j}},w_{4}\right\rangle+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})\left\langle e_{x_{j}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{j}}w_{2}\right\rangle+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})\left\langle u_{y_{j}},w_{4}\right\rangle+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})\left\langle e_{x_{i}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{i}}w_{2}\right\rangle+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})\left\langle u_{y_{i}},w_{4}\right\rangle~," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.330em">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})\left\langle e_{x_{i}},w_{1}\right\rangle+\left\langle e_{y_{i}}w_{2}\right\rangle+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})\left\langle u_{y_{i}},w_{4}\right\rangle~,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">which is a contradiction to (<a href="#A5.E39" title="Equation 39 ‣ Proof. ‣ E.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) and <span id="A5.SS3.p1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">(<a href="#A5.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ Proof. ‣ E.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix E Theoretical analysis ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>)</span>. This means that there is no linear separator, regardless of the values of the parameters, which proves the first item.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume there is layer normalization after the prediction as in (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Setup. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).
This means that the output of the model is <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{v}{\left\lVert v\right\rVert}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{v}{\left\lVert v\right\rVert}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the linear predictor <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a bias term <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> that will be determined later. Then, the output of the linear predictor is exactly <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle w,v\right\rangle=\frac{1}{\left\lVert v\right\rVert}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle w,v\right\rangle=\frac{1}{\left\lVert v\right\rVert}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We will now calculate the norm of both true and false samples. For a true sample <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,g(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,g(x))</annotation></semantics></math> we have that:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2+(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})^{2}\cdot(2N-1)+\left(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}+\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}\right)^{2}~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2+(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})^{2}\cdot(2N-1)+\left(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}+\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}\right)^{2}~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For a negative sample <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)\neq y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)\neq y</annotation></semantics></math> we have:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2+\alpha_{1}^{2}+\alpha_{2}^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})^{2}\cdot(2N-2)+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}+\beta_{1})^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}-\beta_{2})^{2}~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2+\alpha_{1}^{2}+\alpha_{2}^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})^{2}\cdot(2N-2)+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}+\beta_{1})^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}-\beta_{2})^{2}~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">There exists a linear separator as long as <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert}-\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert}-\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the vectors <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> are both non-zero, this is equivalent to <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}\neq\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}\neq\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the above calculation, we have that:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}-\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}-\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{1}^{2}+\alpha_{2}^{2}-(\alpha_{1}-\alpha_{2})^{2}-(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}+\beta_{1})^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}-\beta_{2})^{2}-(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}+\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{1}^{2}+\alpha_{2}^{2}-(\alpha_{1}-\alpha_{2})^{2}-(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2})^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}+\beta_{1})^{2}+(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}-\beta_{2})^{2}-(\gamma_{1}-\gamma_{2}+\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}+2\beta_{1}\beta_{2}~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}+2\beta_{1}\beta_{2}~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that if <math id="A5.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}+2\beta_{1}\beta_{2}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}+2\beta_{1}\beta_{2}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> then we have a linear separation between true and false samples.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Further assuming that <math id="A5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}=\alpha_{2},~\beta_{1}=\beta_{2},~\gamma_{1}=\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}=\alpha_{2},~\beta_{1}=\beta_{2},~\gamma_{1}=\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> we have that <math id="A5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}=2+2\alpha_{2}+2\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}=2+2\alpha_{2}+2\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To find the optimal margin for this predictor we pick:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert}-\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert}\right)=\frac{1}{2\sqrt{2}}\left(1-\frac{1}{\sqrt{1+\alpha^{2}+\beta^{2}}}\right)~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert}-\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert}\right)=\frac{1}{2\sqrt{2}}\left(1-\frac{1}{\sqrt{1+\alpha^{2}+\beta^{2}}}\right)~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We will now prove that there is linear separation after predicting the <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> token. Using the output of the model as in (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Setup. ‣ 4 Analysis on a Toy Model ‣ Emergence of Linear Truth Encodings in Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) we get:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{T}=C+\frac{1}{3}\left((\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})e_{x}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})u_{y}-\alpha_{1}e_{x^{\prime}}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x^{\prime})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{T}=C+\frac{1}{3}\left((\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})e_{x}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2})u_{y}-\alpha_{1}e_{x^{\prime}}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x^{\prime})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{F}=C+\frac{1}{3}\left(-\alpha_{1}e_{x}+\alpha_{2}u_{g^{-1}(y)}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}-\beta_{2}u_{y}+-\alpha_{1}e_{x^{\prime}}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x^{\prime})}\right)~," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.330em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{F}=C+\frac{1}{3}\left(-\alpha_{1}e_{x}+\alpha_{2}u_{g^{-1}(y)}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x)}-\beta_{2}u_{y}+-\alpha_{1}e_{x^{\prime}}+\beta_{1}u_{g(x^{\prime})}\right)~,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=e_{x^{\prime}}+p_{3}+\frac{\hat{\gamma}}{3}\cdot\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=e_{x^{\prime}}+p_{3}+\frac{\hat{\gamma}}{3}\cdot\left(\sum_{y}u_{y}-\sum_{x}u_{x}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. We can now calculate:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}=2+\frac{1}{9}\left((\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})^{2}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+\alpha_{1}^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(2N-2)\bar{\gamma}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}=2+\frac{1}{9}\left((\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})^{2}+(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+\alpha_{1}^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(2N-2)\bar{\gamma}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}=2+\frac{1}{9}\left(2\alpha_{1}^{2}+\alpha_{2}^{2}+2(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\bar{\gamma}-\beta_{2})^{2}+(2N-3)\bar{\gamma}^{2}\right)~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}=2+\frac{1}{9}\left(2\alpha_{1}^{2}+\alpha_{2}^{2}+2(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\bar{\gamma}-\beta_{2})^{2}+(2N-3)\bar{\gamma}^{2}\right)~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">We now have that:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}-\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert^{2}-\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex87.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{9}\cdot\left(\alpha_{1}^{2}+\alpha_{2}^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\bar{\gamma}-\beta_{2})^{2}-(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})^{2}-(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}-\bar{\gamma}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{9}\cdot\left(\alpha_{1}^{2}+\alpha_{2}^{2}+(\beta_{1}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}+(\bar{\gamma}-\beta_{2})^{2}-(\alpha_{2}-\alpha_{1})^{2}-(\beta_{1}-\beta_{2}+\bar{\gamma})^{2}-\bar{\gamma}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2}{9}(\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}+\beta_{1}\beta_{2})~." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2}{9}(\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}+\beta_{1}\beta_{2})~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">By a similar argument to the previous case, if <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}+\beta_{1}\beta_{2}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}\alpha_{2}+\beta_{1}\beta_{2}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> then there is linear separation between true and false samples. Further assuming that <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}=\alpha_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}=\alpha_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\gamma}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\gamma}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, to find the optimal margin for the predictor we pick:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert}-\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert}\right)=\frac{\alpha^{2}+\beta^{2}}{9\sqrt{4+\frac{8}{9}(\alpha^{2}+\beta^{2})+\frac{1}{27}(\alpha^{2}+\beta^{2})^{2}}}~." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{T}\right\rVert}-\frac{1}{\left\lVert v_{F}\right\rVert}\right)=\frac{\alpha^{2}+\beta^{2}}{9\sqrt{4+\frac{8}{9}(\alpha^{2}+\beta^{2})+\frac{1}{27}(\alpha^{2}+\beta^{2})^{2}}}~.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Evaluating checkpoints of a “real” LM</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To test whether the two-phase dynamics also appear in a large model trained on open-web data, we analyzed the <span id="A5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pythia-6.9B</span> training checkpoints released by EleutherAI. Using the <span id="A5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CounterFact</span> dataset we construct each input by concatenating <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=4</annotation></semantics></math> factual statements whose preceding context is either entirely true or entirely false, mirroring our previous setup. For every checkpoint we measure three signals on the final statement:</p>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Memorization</span>: percentage of cases where greedy decoding succeeds in completing the correct token.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Uncertainty</span>: entropy of the model’s full-vocabulary distribution for predicting the last token; we record the difference between true and false context.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Linear separability</span>: accuracy of a linear probe trained to classify the truth value of the surrounding context.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
